*Heading
An *EQUATION whose first DOF also has a *BOUNDARY (an overconstraint ccx rejects)
** A C3D8 cube, clamped at x = 0 and pulled at x = 1 by 10 per node.  The *Equation ties
** u_x of the clamped node 1 to u_x of the free node 2; ccx eliminates the FIRST term of an
** equation, and node 1 DOF 1 is also under the BC, so ccx stops ('*ERROR in cascade: ...
** dependent side of a MPC and a SPC').  Abaqus resolves this; abq2ccx lists the terms the
** other way round (the same equation) so node 2 DOF 1 is the eliminated one, and drops the
** duplicate equation that follows (no DOF of it is free, and it holds anyway).
** The last three equations tie u_x of nodes 3, 6, 7 in a loop; ccx accepts that, but finds
** a zero coefficient on the last one's dependent side and silently holds all three at
** u_x = 0.  The loop's closing equation follows from the other two, so abq2ccx drops it.
** Expected: node 2 stays at u_x = 0; nodes 3, 6 and 7 move in +x by one common amount.
